  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given an arithmetic sequence that has ${a}_{3}=-5$ and common difference $d=2,$ what is the index of the term $99?$",
  "worked_solution": "Since ${a}_{3}=-5$ is $2$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={a}_{1}+2d \\\\ -5 & ={a}_{1}+2(2) \\\\ -5 & ={a}_{1}+4 \\\\ -9 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-9+(n-1)(2) \\\\  & =-9+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=99,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2n-11 \\\\ 99 & =2n-11 \\\\ 110 & =2n \\\\ \\frac{110}{2} & =n \\\\ 55 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $99$ is the $55$th term of the sequence.",
